`opus-pure` is a pure-Rust port of the reference libopus implementation (via
`rusty-opus` and `opus-rs`, both BSD-3-Clause); its `ATTRIBUTION.md` records
that chain and we carry its inherited notices above rather than only the
most recent one. No libopus C source is vendored, built or linked, and no
Plaudon source is derived from it.

BSD-3-Clause requires that the copyright notice, the list of conditions and
the disclaimer are reproduced with a binary redistribution; the full licence
text ships with the crate (`LICENSE`) and is reproduced in the release
evidence bundle. The Opus format itself is an IETF standard (RFC 6716,
RFC 7845) and carries no additional notice obligation.

